{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmJEW7ooEyULF4vC5zyF", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "In the repo, yes: I didn't change anything about alerting. `config/review.cfg` still has `no_notify = false`, the same threshold (2) and the same recipients, and `pipeline/notify.py` and `pipeline/review.py` are untouched. `git status` is clean.\n\nIn practice, though, two things mean alerts aren't working right now:\n\n1. **I held back alerts for the 2026-11-04 rerun.** That run used a temporary config copy with `no_notify = true`, which only lasted for that one run. Because of it, the severity 3 finding (the agent writing to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`) never reached anyone. Last night's original run crashed before the alert step, so this finding hasn't alerted anyone at any point. Someone needs to forward it by hand.\n\n2. **The nightly job can't send alerts until the findings path is fixed.** In `review.run`, the findings directory is created before any alerts go out. So while `/srv/acme/review-findings` can't be written, every nightly run will crash before alerting, and publishing will fail too. Alerting comes back once the volume is set up on the runner or `findings_dir` points back to a writable path."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "64b72b83-208e-406a-aa39-1ec9c9800b2b", "uuid": "f8aa4b31-a7fd-40ef-9785-578bcad50fad", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T07:42:06.561Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmJEVqh9Fs2tjuWiRLVR"}
